WEBVTT

1
01:02:33.282 --> 01:02:38.282
A block of concrete has been laid upon you, I understand.

2
01:02:38.282 --> 01:02:42.082
Dear Father in heaven, I thank you for who you are.

3
01:02:42.082 --> 01:02:46.082
You are the risen Lord Jesus and we believe in you.

4
01:02:46.082 --> 01:02:52.282
We believe in you and I want to pray in the name of Jesus that everyone who is in this room,

5
01:02:52.282 --> 01:02:56.082
will draw closer to you, even through this sermon.

6
01:02:56.082 --> 01:03:00.082
That people will learn that you are the risen Lord.

7
01:03:00.082 --> 01:03:04.482
And that you are true and that you are holy and that you are King.

8
01:03:04.482 --> 01:03:09.282
You are the King of Kings and we love you Jesus.

9
01:03:09.282 --> 01:03:15.282
And I bless everyone in the name of Jesus that the Word of God will take shape in your heart.

10
01:03:15.282 --> 01:03:21.082
And that it will bring a change that will make you more and more like Christ, in Jesus' name.

11
01:03:21.082 --> 01:03:25.082
Amen. Amen. Glory to God. Hallelujah.

12
01:03:26.082 --> 01:03:32.082
Today is Ascension... no, not today is Ascension.

13
01:03:32.082 --> 01:03:37.082
Next Thursday is Ascension. Right?

14
01:03:37.082 --> 01:03:44.082
And Ascension is forty days after the resurrection of Jesus.

15
01:03:44.082 --> 01:03:49.082
And what I want to teach you today is the fact...

16
01:03:50.082 --> 01:03:57.082
I want to teach today about the simple subject that the ascension of Jesus...

17
01:03:57.082 --> 01:04:03.082
is a real event that happened physically and truly.

18
01:04:03.082 --> 01:04:09.082
And I will explain to you why this is so important for our faith. Right?

19
01:04:09.082 --> 01:04:13.082
So next Thursday is Ascension.

20
01:04:13.082 --> 01:04:17.082
And this is the way I want to explain it.

21
01:04:17.082 --> 01:04:24.082
Can you still remember that I talked about those two men who were walking on that road and had an encounter with Jesus?

22
01:04:26.082 --> 01:04:30.082
What I am about to read is the extended part of that.

23
01:04:30.082 --> 01:04:39.082
So Jesus was nailed to a cross, killed by men, but he gave life.

24
01:04:39.082 --> 01:04:43.082
No one could kill him. He gave life, says the Bible.

25
01:04:43.082 --> 01:04:51.082
That is an important thing. Jesus says about himself that the Son of Man has the authority to lay down his life...

26
01:04:51.082 --> 01:04:54.082
and to take it up again whenever he wants.

27
01:04:54.082 --> 01:04:59.082
Therefore, he has authority over all names. Amen?

28
01:04:59.082 --> 01:05:05.082
And those two men from Emmaus who saw Jesus walking...

29
01:05:05.082 --> 01:05:10.082
these two men saw him in physical form.

30
01:05:11.082 --> 01:05:19.082
And we need to take the time for this because the Bible apparently mentions a considerable number of situations...

31
01:05:19.082 --> 01:05:28.082
and takes the time and takes something very seriously to show that Jesus Christ has truly risen.

32
01:05:28.082 --> 01:05:37.082
That he has risen physically. Just like me, a human, fully of flesh and blood.

33
01:05:37.082 --> 01:05:46.082
The Bible is indeed full of a number of different types of genres.

34
01:05:46.082 --> 01:05:49.082
One genre is about how you should read something.

35
01:05:49.082 --> 01:05:55.082
For example, poetry is a separate genre from history.

36
01:05:55.082 --> 01:06:00.082
Something that has historically happened must also be read factually.

37
01:06:00.082 --> 01:06:02.082
That is how it happened.

38
01:06:02.082 --> 01:06:05.082
When the Bible, for example, shows years...

39
01:06:05.082 --> 01:06:10.082
this king lived at that time and this happened then...

40
01:06:10.082 --> 01:06:15.082
then the Bible wants to indicate, this is the genre of historical fact.

41
01:06:15.082 --> 01:06:21.082
When the Bible shows in the psalms that God is our rock on which we can build...

42
01:06:21.082 --> 01:06:25.082
then you must read that in the genre of poetry.

43
01:06:25.082 --> 01:06:29.082
So that you don't start thinking that God is a piece of stone that you live on...

44
01:06:29.082 --> 01:06:35.082
but you understand that the poetry and its depth is that you can always trust God.

45
01:06:35.082 --> 01:06:36.082
Amen?

46
01:06:36.082 --> 01:06:39.082
So the Bible is full of different genres.

47
01:06:39.082 --> 01:06:44.082
Prophecy, history, even myth.

48
01:06:44.082 --> 01:06:50.082
And then you have history and the things that actually happened.

49
01:06:50.082 --> 01:06:54.082
So when you read something that can be symbolic...

50
01:06:54.082 --> 01:07:00.082
it can be difficult for us humans to differentiate...

51
01:07:00.082 --> 01:07:05.082
between what is symbolism and what is history.

52
01:07:05.082 --> 01:07:07.082
That is not always easy.

53
01:07:07.082 --> 01:07:09.082
Here is a key that I want to give you.

54
01:07:09.082 --> 01:07:15.082
When the Bible repeats different situations...

55
01:07:15.082 --> 01:07:20.082
to say something again and again and again...

56
01:07:20.082 --> 01:07:22.082
but all in a different kind of story...

57
01:07:22.082 --> 01:07:27.082
then the Bible wants to indicate, listen, you need to think carefully about this...

58
01:07:27.082 --> 01:07:30.082
this really happened.

59
01:07:30.082 --> 01:07:33.082
Understand this well?

60
01:07:33.082 --> 01:07:36.082
For example, two men are walking on a road...

61
01:07:36.082 --> 01:07:42.082
and they are crying and acting all sad about the fact that Jesus has died.

62
01:07:42.082 --> 01:07:46.082
Jesus taught all about the kingdom of God...

63
01:07:46.082 --> 01:07:51.082
and all of a sudden our Lord dies on a cross and now everything is over.

64
01:07:51.082 --> 01:07:53.082
And these two men are crying...

65
01:07:53.082 --> 01:07:57.082
because poof, all their faith and all their hope was completely shattered.

66
01:07:57.082 --> 01:08:00.082
And all of a sudden Jesus walks with them.

67
01:08:00.082 --> 01:08:03.082
And then they think, oh what is going on here?

68
01:08:03.082 --> 01:08:07.082
And then the Bible says, and Jesus came with them and sat down at the table with them...

69
01:08:07.082 --> 01:08:10.082
and he broke the bread and he ate it.

70
01:08:10.082 --> 01:08:15.082
This is indeed a physical gesture of a physical man...

71
01:08:15.082 --> 01:08:20.082
who is physically present and can physically eat.

72
01:08:20.082 --> 01:08:24.082
Because ghosts cannot eat, you understand that.

73
01:08:24.082 --> 01:08:28.082
The Bible is serious about this.

74
01:08:28.082 --> 01:08:31.082
There is another story that points to this...

75
01:08:31.082 --> 01:08:36.082
that we must take the resurrection of the physical form of Jesus literally...

76
01:08:36.082 --> 01:08:40.082
and not spiritually or symbolically or philosophically.

77
01:08:40.082 --> 01:08:43.082
You must take this literally in your faith.

78
01:08:43.082 --> 01:08:47.082
Another story is that one of the disciples, Thomas...

79
01:08:47.082 --> 01:08:53.082
was not present at one of the appearances of the risen Lord.

80
01:08:53.082 --> 01:08:57.082
And the brothers came to Thomas and they said...

81
01:08:57.082 --> 01:09:01.082
Thomas, Thomas, Jesus has truly risen.

82
01:09:01.082 --> 01:09:05.082
And Thomas loved the Lord so much.

83
01:09:05.082 --> 01:09:08.082
He loved God so much.

84
01:09:08.082 --> 01:09:12.082
That he said, I love him so much and I am in so much pain over his death.

85
01:09:12.082 --> 01:09:19.082
I cannot believe it unless I see him physically myself.

86
01:09:19.082 --> 01:09:24.082
And at the next appearance, Thomas is also in the room.

87
01:09:24.082 --> 01:09:28.082
And Jesus walks to Thomas and says to Thomas...

88
01:09:28.082 --> 01:09:31.082
Dear Thomas, feel my hands.

89
01:09:31.082 --> 01:09:36.082
And the scars from the holes in his hands and feet were present...

90
01:09:36.082 --> 01:09:40.082
as proof to Thomas that this is Jesus.

91
01:09:40.082 --> 01:09:43.082
Not another person.

92
01:09:43.082 --> 01:09:50.082
Not interchangeable with someone else, so that we say about that other person...

93
01:09:50.082 --> 01:09:55.082
Look, that is Jesus, because the real Jesus is dead in a grave.

94
01:09:55.082 --> 01:09:57.082
This went around.

95
01:09:57.082 --> 01:09:59.082
So you must understand this well.

96
01:09:59.082 --> 01:10:02.082
The real Jesus stands before Thomas and says...

97
01:10:02.082 --> 01:10:05.082
Thomas, feel my hands and feel my feet.

98
01:10:05.082 --> 01:10:08.082
And Thomas falls down in worship before the Lord.

99
01:10:08.082 --> 01:10:12.082
And he says, my Lord, my God.

100
01:10:12.082 --> 01:10:15.082
Do you know what Jesus then says?

101
01:10:15.082 --> 01:10:21.082
You are blessed because you can feel and see this now.

102
01:10:21.082 --> 01:10:27.082
How much more are the people in 2023 blessed...

103
01:10:27.082 --> 01:10:34.082
if they believe in my resurrection, even though they do not see and feel me.

104
01:10:34.082 --> 01:10:41.082
You are blessed even more than the blessing of Thomas...

105
01:10:41.082 --> 01:10:47.082
if you believe that Jesus physically rose from the dead.

106
01:10:47.082 --> 01:10:50.082
And physically also returns to heaven.

107
01:10:50.082 --> 01:10:55.082
Your blessing to believe when you do not yet see...

108
01:10:55.082 --> 01:11:00.082
is a higher faith than being able to truly feel something.

109
01:11:00.082 --> 01:11:03.082
For the evidence of faith...

110
01:11:03.082 --> 01:11:07.082
is that you have hope in the things you do not see.

111
01:11:07.082 --> 01:11:11.082
This is the definition of faith. Amen?

112
01:11:11.082 --> 01:11:15.082
So I am going to tell you the following story...

113
01:11:15.082 --> 01:11:21.082
which shows that the resurrection of Jesus is truly physical.

114
01:11:21.082 --> 01:11:26.082
Luke chapter 24, verses 33 to 53.

115
01:11:26.082 --> 01:11:30.082
They went to the eleven disciples and the people who were with them.

116
01:11:30.082 --> 01:11:32.082
Those were the two men.

117
01:11:32.082 --> 01:11:35.082
They quickly returned. They had walked from Jerusalem.

118
01:11:35.082 --> 01:11:38.082
They went to Emmaus, to that little town.

119
01:11:38.082 --> 01:11:41.082
And they met Jesus there.

120
01:11:41.082 --> 01:11:45.082
Back to the disciples to tell that Jesus truly lives.

121
01:11:45.082 --> 01:11:47.082
So those are the two men.

122
01:11:47.082 --> 01:11:50.082
They went to the eleven disciples and the people who were with them.

123
01:11:50.082 --> 01:11:52.082
And they said to the second...

124
01:11:52.082 --> 01:11:55.082
The disciples responded to those two, as if the second already didn't know.

125
01:11:55.082 --> 01:11:56.082
They just experienced that.

126
01:11:56.082 --> 01:12:01.082
They said to those two, the Lord Jesus has truly risen.

127
01:12:01.082 --> 01:12:05.082
The Bible means truly risen by this.

128
01:12:05.082 --> 01:12:08.082
Simon has seen Him.

129
01:12:08.082 --> 01:12:11.082
And then the two men told what had happened on the way.

130
01:12:11.082 --> 01:12:18.082
And that they had recognized Him when He broke the bread.

131
01:12:18.082 --> 01:12:23.082
And while they were talking about this, Jesus Himself stood...

132
01:12:23.082 --> 01:12:28.082
And the Bible means Himself with them.

133
01:12:28.082 --> 01:12:32.082
And He said, I wish you peace.

134
01:12:32.082 --> 01:12:36.082
But they were terribly frightened and thought they saw a spirit.

135
01:12:36.082 --> 01:12:39.082
We'll come back to that. Sprook!

136
01:12:39.082 --> 01:12:43.082
But He said, why are you so frightened?

137
01:12:43.082 --> 01:12:46.082
And why do you think that?

138
01:12:46.082 --> 01:12:48.082
The Lord sees thoughts.

139
01:12:48.082 --> 01:12:52.082
Look at my hands and my feet.

140
01:12:52.082 --> 01:12:58.082
Then you can see that I am Ego Amy.

141
01:12:58.082 --> 01:13:02.082
That I am the one.

142
01:13:02.082 --> 01:13:05.082
This is master of Lucas.

143
01:13:05.082 --> 01:13:08.082
Ego Amy means I am.

144
01:13:08.082 --> 01:13:11.082
Ego Amy means I am God.

145
01:13:11.082 --> 01:13:16.082
The claim Ego Amy, the Greek word Ego, I, Amy, am...

146
01:13:16.082 --> 01:13:20.082
means that only God could say these two words.

147
01:13:20.082 --> 01:13:24.082
If you were to say at that time a claim Ego Amy...

148
01:13:24.082 --> 01:13:26.082
you would be claiming that you are God.

149
01:13:26.082 --> 01:13:30.082
Then you would be ready for blasphemy and would have to die.

150
01:13:30.082 --> 01:13:34.082
But the truly risen Lord Jesus makes a claim here.

151
01:13:34.082 --> 01:13:37.082
Ego Amy, I am it.

152
01:13:37.082 --> 01:13:39.082
I am the one.

153
01:13:39.082 --> 01:13:46.082
I am the risen man of flesh and blood Jesus of Nazareth.

154
01:13:46.082 --> 01:13:50.082
And I am simultaneously God.

155
01:13:50.082 --> 01:13:52.082
Creator of heaven and earth.

156
01:13:52.082 --> 01:13:54.082
King of kings.

157
01:13:54.082 --> 01:13:56.082
The beginning and the end.

158
01:13:56.082 --> 01:13:58.082
I am who I am.

159
01:13:58.082 --> 01:14:03.082
I was with Moses and I will be at the end of times.

160
01:14:03.082 --> 01:14:06.082
Ego Amy, He says.

161
01:14:06.082 --> 01:14:08.082
And this is so important.

162
01:14:08.082 --> 01:14:12.082
This came in like an atomic bomb into this room.

163
01:14:12.082 --> 01:14:15.082
Just look at my hands and feet.

164
01:14:15.082 --> 01:14:20.082
And then I thank God that God Himself takes the time...

165
01:14:20.082 --> 01:14:26.082
to come and prove Himself to us humans in flesh and blood.

166
01:14:26.082 --> 01:14:30.082
And He does it time and again.

167
01:14:30.082 --> 01:14:33.082
I wish you peace, He says.

168
01:14:33.082 --> 01:14:37.082
What more can Jesus do...

169
01:14:37.082 --> 01:14:40.082
than rise from the dead.

170
01:14:40.082 --> 01:14:43.082
Die on a cross for your and my sin.

171
01:14:43.082 --> 01:14:45.082
Then He rises from the dead.

172
01:14:45.082 --> 01:14:49.082
And He comes in with His power and majesty.

173
01:14:49.082 --> 01:14:51.082
And speaks that peace.

174
01:14:51.082 --> 01:14:54.082
Hallelujah, thank you dear Jesus.

175
01:14:54.082 --> 01:14:58.082
Then you can see that I am the one.

176
01:14:58.082 --> 01:14:59.082
Feel it.

177
01:14:59.082 --> 01:15:03.082
A spirit does not have flesh and bones.

178
01:15:03.082 --> 01:15:05.082
But I do, He says.

179
01:15:05.082 --> 01:15:08.082
And He showed them His hands and His feet.

180
01:15:08.082 --> 01:15:12.082
They were so amazed and happy...

181
01:15:12.082 --> 01:15:14.082
that they could hardly believe it.

182
01:15:14.082 --> 01:15:17.082
And so He said to them...

183
01:15:17.082 --> 01:15:20.082
Here comes the second example to prove...

184
01:15:20.082 --> 01:15:23.082
that He has physically risen from the dead.

185
01:15:23.082 --> 01:15:26.082
So first He says, touch my hands, touch my feet.

186
01:15:26.082 --> 01:15:28.082
The first proof.

187
01:15:28.082 --> 01:15:32.082
And so He says, because they still could not believe it...

188
01:15:32.082 --> 01:15:35.082
He says, okay, okay, I'm up for it.

189
01:15:35.082 --> 01:15:37.082
Do we have another proof that I can do?

190
01:15:37.082 --> 01:15:39.082
I am hungry, says Jesus.

191
01:15:39.082 --> 01:15:42.082
Just let me see...

192
01:15:42.082 --> 01:15:45.082
that there is something to eat, so I can show you...

193
01:15:45.082 --> 01:15:48.082
that Ego Amy is standing here.

194
01:15:48.082 --> 01:15:50.082
Isn't this powerful?

195
01:15:50.082 --> 01:15:52.082
Then He says, do you have anything to eat here?

196
01:15:52.082 --> 01:15:57.082
That's why I always say, when I visit someone...

197
01:15:57.082 --> 01:16:00.082
Do you have anything to eat here?

198
01:16:00.082 --> 01:16:04.082
Because that is just biblical. Amen.

199
01:16:04.082 --> 01:16:06.082
Hallelujah.

200
01:16:06.082 --> 01:16:08.082
Only I dare not say Ego Amy.

201
01:16:08.082 --> 01:16:11.082
That would be quite a stretch.

202
01:16:11.082 --> 01:16:13.082
But do you have something to eat here, that is completely biblical.

203
01:16:13.082 --> 01:16:16.082
So be careful when I come.

204
01:16:16.082 --> 01:16:20.082
They gave Him a piece of baked fish...

205
01:16:20.082 --> 01:16:22.082
and some honey.

206
01:16:22.082 --> 01:16:24.082
He took it...

207
01:16:24.082 --> 01:16:27.082
and they saw how He ate it.

208
01:16:27.082 --> 01:16:29.082
And He said to them...

209
01:16:29.082 --> 01:16:31.082
this is what I told you...

210
01:16:31.082 --> 01:16:33.082
when I was still with you.

211
01:16:33.082 --> 01:16:36.082
Everything that is written about me in the books of Moses...

212
01:16:36.082 --> 01:16:38.082
and of the prophets and in the psalms...

213
01:16:38.082 --> 01:16:40.082
had to happen.

214
01:16:40.082 --> 01:16:42.082
Right?

215
01:16:42.082 --> 01:16:44.082
Pay close attention to what is happening here.

216
01:16:44.082 --> 01:16:50.082
Then He made sure they finally understood the books.

217
01:16:50.082 --> 01:16:53.082
Pay close attention to why I want to give this sermon...

218
01:16:53.082 --> 01:16:55.082
about this one subject.

219
01:16:55.082 --> 01:16:57.082
I do not want to give five subjects.

220
01:16:57.082 --> 01:16:59.082
I do not want to give three lessons.

221
01:16:59.082 --> 01:17:01.082
I have only one lesson to present today.

222
01:17:01.082 --> 01:17:03.082
And that one lesson is...

223
01:17:03.082 --> 01:17:05.082
it is of vital importance...

224
01:17:05.082 --> 01:17:07.082
that you believe...

225
01:17:07.082 --> 01:17:11.082
in the physically deceased person of Jesus on a cross...

226
01:17:11.082 --> 01:17:14.082
in the physical resurrection of Jesus...

227
01:17:14.082 --> 01:17:16.082
from a grave three days later...

228
01:17:16.082 --> 01:17:19.082
and the physical ascension of Jesus...

229
01:17:19.082 --> 01:17:22.082
on the Mount of Olives...

230
01:17:23.082 --> 01:17:25.082
on the Mount of Olives...

231
01:17:25.082 --> 01:17:27.082
physically He returns to heaven.

232
01:17:27.082 --> 01:17:29.082
And why is this important?

233
01:17:29.082 --> 01:17:31.082
I will explain it to you.

234
01:17:31.082 --> 01:17:33.082
Because in verse 45 it says...

235
01:17:33.082 --> 01:17:35.082
if you believe this...

236
01:17:35.082 --> 01:17:40.082
then He made sure they finally understood the books.

237
01:17:40.082 --> 01:17:42.082
Here is my lesson for today.

238
01:17:42.082 --> 01:17:47.082
You can only understand the full Word of God.

239
01:17:47.082 --> 01:17:51.082
You can only believe the whole Bible...

240
01:17:51.082 --> 01:17:56.082
if you believe in the physical resurrection of Jesus.

241
01:17:56.082 --> 01:17:58.082
Why?

242
01:17:58.082 --> 01:18:01.082
Even in Islam...

243
01:18:01.082 --> 01:18:04.082
even in other religions...

244
01:18:04.082 --> 01:18:06.082
and especially in the early days...

245
01:18:06.082 --> 01:18:08.082
in the first century after Christ...

246
01:18:08.082 --> 01:18:11.082
gnosticism rose enormously.

247
01:18:11.082 --> 01:18:14.082
Gnosticism was actually a movement of faith...

248
01:18:14.082 --> 01:18:17.082
that actually taught against the people...

249
01:18:17.082 --> 01:18:20.082
that life is actually more about the spiritual.

250
01:18:20.082 --> 01:18:23.082
It is all spiritual and everything is symbolic.

251
01:18:23.082 --> 01:18:25.082
We are going to sit on a mat...

252
01:18:25.082 --> 01:18:27.082
and we are going to smoke and we are going to enjoy some weed...

253
01:18:27.082 --> 01:18:29.082
because everything is spiritual.

254
01:18:29.082 --> 01:18:31.082
And everything that is not spiritual...

255
01:18:31.082 --> 01:18:34.082
is of secondary importance.

256
01:18:34.082 --> 01:18:36.082
